<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Put</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>put &lt;item&gt; in &lt;container&gt;
put all in &lt;container&gt;
put money in &lt;container&gt;
put &lt;amount&gt; &lt;coins&gt; in &lt;container&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>put brass lantern in bag
put all in chest
put 20 gold in bag
</pre>
<p>This command puts your things inside a container, like a bag or a chest. The 
word in is needed: put lantern bag doesn't work. The container must be open 
(see <a cmd='#'>Help Open</a>), and it only holds so much.
</p><p>You can only put into one container at a time: put &lt;item1&gt; in &lt;item2&gt; in 
&lt;item3&gt; is the same as put &lt;item1&gt; in &lt;item2&gt;. To take things out again, see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Get</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Get</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Open</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Look</a>
</pre>




</div>